1. PLATFORM UPGRADE PATH VALIDATION (Ubuntu 24.04 OS & Agent Steps)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ACTION                  COMMAND / PROCEDURE
Pre-upgrade OS Check    cat /etc/os-release                            Verify host OS is Ubuntu 24.04 BEFORE running v9
Agent Execution Fix     mount -o remount,exec /tmp                     Fix 'permission denied' agent upgrade script flags
Manual Agent Trigger    Via UI: Infrastructure -> Clusters -> Hosts -> [Select Host] -> ACTIONS -> Upgrade Agent
Offline Script Push     sudo ./hpe-vme-agent-upgrade-script.sh         Run unique host-level shell installer directly

2. STORAGE LUN EXPANSION & GFS2 CAPACITY RESIZING
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CATEGORY                COMMAND                                        DESCRIPTION
Block Layer Rescan      sudo iscsiadm -m node -R                       Force active host session block device capacity rescan
Multipath Extension     sudo multipathd resize map <multipath_device>  Instruct device-mapper to absorb array changes
GFS2 File System Grow   sudo gfs2_grow /mnt/<gfs2_mount_point>         Safely expand the active clustered cluster layout
Capacity Verification   df -hT | grep gfs2                             Verify OS and cluster register the new storage limit

3. POST-UPGRADE POSTURE & QUORUM TROUBLESHOOTING (Layout 1.3 Flags)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Cluster Realignment     sudo hvm-cli cluster status                    Query the native v9 engine for sync locks
Cluster Realignment     sudo hvm-cli host list                         Identify false FENCED or ghost Offline states
Storage Path Validation  ls -la /var/lib/libvirt/qemu/nvram/            Ensure guest Secure Boot NVRAM paths sync across GFS2
